      "abstract": "One of the first new European philosophers who turned to understanding the ancient distinction between entity and being was Hegel. The aim of the article is to analyze how Hegel distinguished entity and being, and does the Hegelian understanding of the difference between entity and being coincide with the Aristotelian tradition? On the basis of the study, it can be concluded that Hegel came close to formulating the fundamental ontological difference, but never completed this task to the end. In our opinion, the undoubted and great merit of Hegel in the \u226aScience of Logic\u226b is the demonstration of the unity and omnipotence of entity in all its manifestations. for Hegel, being is not identical with thinking, and he only hints at the difference between entity and being, without clearly realizing it, and often for him being is not at all different from entity-itself-in-itself.",
