      "paperId": "11565e9e17856b0534bd93b882e54b3234bf09fd",
      "title": "The first Marxist reflection of Georg Luk\u00e1cs",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Jiayang Qin",
          "authorId": "2114048072"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2023,
      "abstract": "The article \u2018Aesthetic culture\u2019 was written in 1908. Although it is in the same period as Soul and Form, in essence, the ideas expressed in this article go beyond the pure philosophy of life and the theory of form, which is different from the idealistic tendency of Luk\u00e1cs in this period. Moreover, \u2018Aesthetic culture\u2019 and History and Class Consciousness have ontological and epistemological consistency in subject\u2013object relation and class consciousness. This was the first Marxist reflection of Luk\u00e1cs, and also a reliable sign that he was to join the Hungarian Communist Party 10 years later and turned to Marxism. By criticizing the paradox of aesthetic culture itself, Luk\u00e1cs tried to construct a culture as a whole as a category, and tried to solve the deep contradiction between the freedom of consciousness and the passive form of the subject in modern society. This kind of culture as a whole would be based on the class consciousness of the proletariat itself and take life as the main category, so as to provide the proletariat with practical theoretical conception to expand their space for living in bourgeois culture.",
